<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 28.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 28.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Thursday published the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period March 26 to 28.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = millon cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 26 (actual) 237 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 27 (forecast) 233 mcm, 54 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 28 (forecast) 230 mcm, 54 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 26 (actual) 9.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 27 (forecast) 9.3 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.5 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 28 (forecast) 7.0 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.6 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
